# Always revalidate HTML and JS so deploys take effect immediately.
# (Stale cached JS was causing fixes to never load in the browser.)
#
# July 16 · a blank-cockpit hotfix deployed and STILL did not reach anyone. The apex answered
# `cache-status: "Netlify Edge"; hit` with a climbing `age` (741s, then 819s) while the published
# deploy already contained the fix. Plain `Cache-Control` is what the BROWSER sees and Netlify's
# edge honours it too, but the edge kept serving hits without revalidating, so shipping a deploy
# could not flush it and there is no purge button available to us.
# `Netlify-CDN-Cache-Control` targets Netlify's CDN specifically and takes precedence there over
# the shared `Cache-Control`. HTML and JS here are small and change constantly, and a stale
# cockpit is a broken cockpit, so the edge must never hold them.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  Netlify-CDN-Cache-Control: no-store
/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  Netlify-CDN-Cache-Control: no-store
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Allow the Agent Hub to embed the agent Portal page (My files / Production) in an iframe.
# Scoped to this one page only — does not affect the rest of the site.
/portal.html
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://hub.joinaari.com

